🔎 Nmap
🎯 Purpose
Nmap (Network Mapper) is an open-source command-line tool used for network discovery, port scanning, service version detection, and vulnerability auditing. It helps security professionals identify active hosts, open network ports, running services, and potential entry points across a network.
🧠 Key Concepts
Host Discovery: Identifying live hosts on a network (e.g., via ICMP echo requests, TCP SYN/ACK probes).
Port Scanning States:
`Open`: An application is actively accepting connections on the port.
`Closed`: The port is accessible, but no application is listening.
`Filtered`: A firewall or network filter prevents probes from reaching the port.
Scan Types:
`SYN Scan (-sS)`: Default stealth scan; sends SYN packets without completing the TCP 3-way handshake.
`TCP Connect Scan (-sT)`: Completes the full TCP 3-way handshake; used when non-root privileges prevent raw socket creation.
`UDP Scan (-sU)`: Scans UDP ports (slower due to stateless packet handling).
Nmap Scripting Engine (NSE): Extensible Lua scripts used for advanced service detection, vulnerability checks, and automated reconnaissance.
💻 Commands
```
# Basic Host Discovery (Ping Sweep)
nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24

# Default TCP SYN Scan (Top 1000 ports)
sudo nmap -sS 192.168.1.10

# Scan Specific Ports or Port Ranges
nmap -p 80,443,8080 192.168.1.10
nmap -p 1-65535 192.168.1.10

# Service Version and OS Detection
sudo nmap -sV -O 192.168.1.10

# Aggressive Scan (Enable OS detection, version scanning, script scanning, traceroute)
sudo nmap -A 192.168.1.10

# Output Options (Normal, XML, Grepable, or All Formats)
nmap -sS 192.168.1.10 -oA scan_results

```
📋 Examples
Comprehensive Vulnerability Assessment Scan:
```
  sudo nmap -sC -sV -p- -T4 10.10.10.50 -oA target_full_scan
  
  ```
Running Specific NSE Scripts:
```
  nmap --script vuln 192.168.1.10
  nmap --script http-enum -p 80 192.168.1.10
  
  ```
🔎 Investigation
Identify Unnecessary Services: Look for non-standard open ports (e.g., SSH running on port 2222, web interface on port 8443) that increase attack surface.
Audit Service Versions: Match detected service software versions against known CVE databases to evaluate patch status.
Detect Network Controls: Use `-Pn` (skip host discovery) when target firewalls drop ICMP probes to ensure hidden hosts are still scanned.
⚠️ Important
Privileges: SYN scans (`-sS`) and OS detection (`-O`) require elevated root or `sudo` privileges to manipulate raw network sockets.
Performance & Impact: High timing templates (`-T5`) or scanning all ports (`-p-`) can overload weak network devices or trigger intrusion prevention alarms.
Authorization: Scanning networks without explicit permission is illegal and prohibited outside authorized lab environments or scope agreements.
🛡️ Security
Configure network firewalls to filter unnecessary inbound traffic and block unauthorized probes.
Disable or restrict unnecessary open services on network interfaces to reduce the attack surface.
